{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018F1R3EVQgVfcvNnBWMsF2x","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"}]\n\nI found information about CoRL 2026, though the search results don't include a dedicated page specifically titled \"reviewer guidelines review form\" for 2026. However, I can share what's available:\n\n**CoRL 2026 Information Found:**\n\nThe main CoRL 2026 website and OpenReview submission portal are available, but the reviewer guidelines page for 2026 doesn't appear to be published yet in the search results. \n\n**Available Resources:**\n\nPapers may be submitted through OpenReview at the link: https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference.\n\n**Related Information:**\n\nThe search results do include reviewer guidelines from CoRL 2023 that emphasize being constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects, suggesting improvements, and accepting diverse views. These past guidelines may provide useful reference for the review process.\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held in Austin, Texas, US on November 9-12, 2026.\n\nIf you're looking for the specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, these may not yet be publicly available. You might want to check the official CoRL 2026 website (corl.org) directly or the OpenReview portal for the most up-to-date information as the review period approaches.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bc8b5d4-ce5c-49d6-b6c0-57df99eac310","uuid":"cce21323-567c-49b7-b9b4-581de0c3b3cb","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:25:02.036Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011eW8y2PhobLsEbACsMk8M2","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"}]},"I found information about CoRL 2026, though the search results don't include a dedicated page specifically titled \"reviewer guidelines review form\" for 2026. However, I can share what's available:\n\n**CoRL 2026 Information Found:**\n\nThe main CoRL 2026 website and OpenReview submission portal are available, but the reviewer guidelines page for 2026 doesn't appear to be published yet in the search results. \n\n**Available Resources:**\n\nPapers may be submitted through OpenReview at the link: https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference.\n\n**Related Information:**\n\nThe search results do include reviewer guidelines from CoRL 2023 that emphasize being constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects, suggesting improvements, and accepting diverse views. These past guidelines may provide useful reference for the review process.\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held in Austin, Texas, US on November 9-12, 2026.\n\nIf you're looking for the specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, these may not yet be publicly available. You might want to check the official CoRL 2026 website (corl.org) directly or the OpenReview portal for the most up-to-date information as the review period approaches."],"durationSeconds":5.849601102}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VWVK9pQ5ad9ZABgdF56LUY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 2024 reviewer guidelines rating scale review criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Area Chair Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ACGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL reviewer guidelines. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## Desk Rejection Criteria\n\nPapers can be desk rejected for one of three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope. More specifically, formatting issues involve papers that are either too long or in an incorrect format, and anonymity violations occur when the main manuscript, supplemental materials, or links provided identify one or more authors. For scope, all CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through either explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\n## Review Criteria\n\nKey review criteria include relevance—whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method or learned model, evaluates methods in simulation or on real robots, and whether the CoRL audience will be interested in reading it.\n\n## General Reviewer Expectations\n\nReviewers are expected to be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, suggest improvements, and accept diverse views in discussion.\n\nUnfortunately, the search results did not provide specific information about a numerical rating scale for CoRL 2025 or 2024 reviews. For more detailed rating scale information, you may need to check the official CoRL website or OpenReview platform directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bc8b5d4-ce5c-49d6-b6c0-57df99eac310","uuid":"449fb406-d071-441b-a3aa-b38210594edf","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:25:03.927Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 2024 reviewer guidelines rating scale review criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01EXzsoGTCvpr6U3CCBbhp7Q","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"Area Chair Guidelines","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ACGuide"},{"title":"CoRL Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL reviewer guidelines. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## Desk Rejection Criteria\n\nPapers can be desk rejected for one of three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope. More specifically, formatting issues involve papers that are either too long or in an incorrect format, and anonymity violations occur when the main manuscript, supplemental materials, or links provided identify one or more authors. For scope, all CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through either explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\n## Review Criteria\n\nKey review criteria include relevance—whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method or learned model, evaluates methods in simulation or on real robots, and whether the CoRL audience will be interested in reading it.\n\n## General Reviewer Expectations\n\nReviewers are expected to be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, suggest improvements, and accept diverse views in discussion.\n\nUnfortunately, the search results did not provide specific information about a numerical rating scale for CoRL 2025 or 2024 reviews. For more detailed rating scale information, you may need to check the official CoRL website or OpenReview platform directly."],"durationSeconds":6.671542196999999}}
