{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0145DUHKNTRnfFFMpCyNmgHB","type":"tool_result","content":"# Review Form Fields and Criteria - CoRL 2024\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, I cannot extract a complete review form with specific rating scales or numbered evaluation dimensions. The page titled \"Instruction for Reviews\" does not contain this detailed information.\n\n## What IS Available:\n\n**Review Criteria for Regular Papers:**\nThe document specifies that submissions will be assessed on:\n- \"significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\"\n- \"degree to which they have been objectively established\"\n- \"potential for scientific and technological impact\"\n- \"relevance to robotic learning\"\n\n**Desk Rejection Criteria:**\nPapers may be rejected for formatting issues, anonymity violations, or scope concerns. Scope requires that submissions either \"Explicitly address a learning question for physical robots OR Test the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\"\n\n## Missing Information:\n\nThe webpage does not provide:\n- Specific numerical rating scales (e.g., 1-10)\n- Detailed scale descriptions for individual dimensions\n- Overall recommendation scales\n- Scoring rubrics for soundness, novelty, clarity, or other evaluation metrics\n- The actual review form template\n\nTo obtain the complete review form fields and rating scales, you would need to access CoRL 2024's submission system or contact the conference organizers directly."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bc8b5d4-ce5c-49d6-b6c0-57df99eac310","uuid":"e3ec7b09-e5f1-4cef-8977-a19dd39a23e1","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:25:36.736Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":133929,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Review Form Fields and Criteria - CoRL 2024\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, I cannot extract a complete review form with specific rating scales or numbered evaluation dimensions. The page titled \"Instruction for 