{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NkCfLxgE5dBuT6WPprL3dd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\ttier: worst\n2\tnarrative_guidance: 'Claim 2 collapses — rank-48 universal LoRA nearly matches Meta-Brain\n3\t  (<1pp gap), and random routing performs within 2pp of PAR routing, indicating the\n4\t  multi-expert advantage is primarily an ensemble/capacity effect rather than perturbation-type\n5\t  specialization. Cross-type expert drops are small (3-6pp), confirming experts learn\n6\t  largely interchangeable corrections. The oracle gap (6pp) hints at unrealized potential,\n7\t  but current expert training cannot produce sufficiently specialized adapters to\n8\t  exploit the diagnostic signal. Clean LIBERO shows measurable degradation (-4pp).\n9\t  Radical reframing required: lead with Phase 0 mechanistic finding as primary contribution,\n10\t  present routing experiments as an honest negative result, and position the oracle\n11\t  gap as an open problem. Paper becomes \"diagnostic tools for VLA robustness\" rather\n12\t  than \"routing-based correction.\"\n13\t\n14\t  '\n15\timagined_experiments:\n16\t- name: LoRA expert training — 3 perturbation-specific + 1 universal baseline\n17\t  plan_id: plan_002\n18\t  description: 'Train 4 LoRA adapters (rank 16, ~3.7M each) on frozen pi0 PaliGemma\n19\t    attention layers. LoRA-V on visual augmented data, LoRA-S on spatial perturbation\n20\t    rollouts, LoRA-P on physical perturbation rollouts, Universal on mixed data. Evaluate\n21\t    each on own type and cross-type.\n22\t\n23\t    '\n24\t  expected_results:\n25\t    lora_v_on_visual: 67.0\n26\t    lora_v_on_spatial: 58.0\n27\t    lora_v_on_physical: 49.5\n28\t    lora_s_on_visual: 62.5\n29\t    lora_s_on_spatial: 62.0\n30\t    lora_s_on_physical: 50.0\n31\t    lora_p_on_visual: 61.0\n32\t    lora_p_on_spatial: 57.5\n33\t    lora_p_on_physical: 55.5\n34\t    universal_r16_on_visual: 61.5\n35\t    universal_r16_on_spatial: 56.0\n36\t    universal_r16_on_physical: 49.0\n37\t    universal_r16_overall: 58.5\n38\t    cross_type_avg_drop_pp: 4.7\n39\t    lora_v_training_loss_final: 0.018\n40\t    lora_s_training_loss_final: 0.022\n41\t    lora_p_training_loss_final: 0.031\n42\t    convergence_epochs_v: 12\n43\t    convergence_epochs_s: 18\n44\t    convergence_epochs_p: 25\n45\t  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，专家之间的交叉类型性能下降很小（平均 ~4.7pp），核心原因是 LoRA rank 16 的容量不足以学到真正类型特异性的修正模式。各专家在自身类型上的优势主要来自训练数据分布\n46\t    匹配，而非学到了质性不同的修正函数。LoRA-V 在 Visual 上最强（67%）是因为视觉增强的 训练范式（FTM 式）天然适配 LoRA 微调，但当\n47\t    LoRA-S 被错误应用于 Visual 时仍达 62.5% （仅降 4.5pp），说明 LoRA-S 学到的修正在空间上和视觉修正高度重叠。Physical\n48\t    类型整体 最弱（LoRA-P 仅 55.5%），因为物理扰动改变了力学和接触动态，需要更深层的动作策略调整， 而不仅是表征修正。Universal LoRA\n49\t    r16 的整体 58.5% 已经接近各专家在自身类型上的平均水平， 进一步证实容量而非路由是主要瓶颈。\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0162wxMnazXnfeReKpiWhzih","session_id":"7bc8b5d4-ce5c-49d6-b6c0-57df99eac310","uuid":"53150ce8-12f2-4c06-a0f7-74defab33b40","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:27:45.652Z"}
